    "text": "Here's the implementation of the function `is_simple_power` function in Python:\n\n```python\ndef is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Function is_simple_power that returns True if a number is a power of n and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    def is_simple_power(x, n):\n        return x == n ** n\n    return is_simple_power(x, n)\n```\n\n### Usage:\nis_simple_power(1, 4)  # True\nis_simple_power(2, 2)  # True\nis_simple_power(8, 2)  # True\nis_simple_power(3, 2)  # False\nis_simple_power(3, 1)  # False\nis_simple_power(5, 3)  # False\n```\n\nThis function uses the `**` operator to calculate the `n` power of `n` and compares it directly to `x`.",
